<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="71989" href="schedule/2019/fall/IE/598/71989.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2019" href="schedule/2019.xml">2019</calendarYear><term id="120198" href="schedule/2019/fall.xml">Fall 2019</term><subject id="IE" href="schedule/2019/fall/IE.xml">Industrial Engineering</subject><course id="598" href="schedule/2019/fall/IE/598.xml">Special Topics</course></parents><sectionNumber>EFF</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Estimation &amp; Filtering in Fin</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Prerequisites: IE 410 or equivalent course on stochastic processes. The focus of this course is on optimal online estimation and filtering methods for partially observed dynamical systems, such as Sequential Monte Carlo, MCMC, SMC2, and Particle MCMC. We will apply these techniques to the study of the volatility of a stock or an index. More specifically, we will introduce discrete and continuous time stochastic volatility models and study the dynamics of the volatility surface.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2019-08-26Z</startDate><endDate>2019-12-11Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LEC">Lecture</type><start>02:00 PM</start><end>03:20 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>1302</roomNumber><buildingName>Siebel Center for Comp Sci</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Chronopoulou" firstName="A">Chronopoulou, A</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>